Run one of the commands treerig.toml declares under [commands], in this
registered worktree, with the worktree's TREERIG_* environment and
TREERIG_COMMAND naming it. Everything after -- is passed to the command. It runs
on the terminal, so it can prompt and answer Ctrl-C itself, and its output is
this command's own; its exit code becomes treerig run's. Unless it sets lock =
false, it holds the worktree's lock while it runs. docs/hooks.md has the
details.

Usage:
  treerig run [name] [-- args...] [flags]

Flags:
      --config string   path to treerig.toml (default: nearest above cwd)
  -h, --help            help for run

Global Flags:
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail
